# Schema conventions (fixture)

An inert trim of the clauses the two-revision gate reads. The normative
document is `notes/plan/schemas/README.md`; this copy exists so a fixture pair
can state which freeze regime it is written under.

## What advances a schema epoch

`schema_epoch` is a breaking-change counter, not a release counter. A change to
a schema document MUST advance `schema_epoch` when it can invalidate an
instance that was valid before, or change what a valid instance means.

The interface is frozen (plan §25): a published document is immutable, and a
breaking change mints `v<n+1>` and leaves `v<n>` byte-for-byte intact.
